        "answer": "No. The tsumitate quota has no separate ¥6 million lifetime limit. Under the new NISA (in force since 1 January 2024) the total lifetime limit is ¥18,000,000, measured at purchase cost. Only the growth quota has a sub-cap (¥12,000,000). The tsumitate quota can fill the whole ¥18,000,000 by itself. Its annual limit is ¥1,200,000. ¥6,000,000 was the old general NISA total (¥1.2M × 5 years). The old tsumitate NISA limit was ¥8,000,000 (¥400,000 × 20 years).",
