          "cacheRead": 21876,
          "cacheWrite": 0,
          "output": 1135
        },
        "answer": "**No, not yet.** As of 2026-10-05, a 10-year-old cannot open a NISA account. From 2024 to 2026 there is no NISA option for minors. Junior NISA is closed to new investment, and adult NISA requires age 18 or older on January 1.\n\nChildren's NISA (こどもNISA) is enacted law (令和8年法律第12号) but not yet in force. It starts **January 1, 2027** for residents aged 0–17. Limits are ¥600,000 a year and ¥6,000,000 lifetime, and it is tsumitate-type investment trusts only. Withdrawals are blocked under age 12. Your child would be eligible then, if aged 17 or under on January 1, 2027. Institutions and opening procedures are still to be announced by the FSA.",
